<p>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Sunday that Israel was close to completing a stated war aim in Gaza: killing those it says planned the Oct. 7, 2023, Hamas-led attacks on southern Israel. His remarks followed the Israeli military’s announcement that an Israeli airstrike killed Izz al-Din al-Haddad, also spelled Ezzedine Al-Haddad, the chief of Hamas’ military wing in Gaza, on Friday. Israel described Haddad as one of the senior Hamas commanders who helped direct the planning and execution of the attacks. Hamas confirmed his death. Netanyahu also said Israeli forces now control 60% of Gaza.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/QS07bgCuBxoPyhuoLvuEI8ksS-IPFrzVPtDeHz2e3HS45zACZEqANWcQiZtBFYFvdA5dxNtn9BXvZa165-IwnRqIzvBQj0zH5wPwYsBmphonjQ' alt='Palestinians place their hands on the body of Izz al-Din al-Haddad, draped in a Hamas flag during his funeral in Gaza City, Saturday, May 16, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Command succession: Israel said Haddad took over Hamas’ military command in Gaza after Mohammed Sinwar was killed, while Business Recorder reported he became military chief after Sinwar’s killing in May 2025.</li><li>Hostage claims: The Israeli military said Haddad surrounded himself with Israeli hostages during the war as protection against attack, a claim reported by AP and carried by WBUR.</li><li>Gaza lines: Reports said Israeli forces had advanced toward a newly drawn “orange line,” beyond the “yellow line” referred to in the U.S.-mediated ceasefire terms.</li><li>Friday strikes: Local medics said at least two Israeli attacks on Gaza on Friday killed seven Palestinians, including three women and one child.</li></ul><blockquote>capture as many soldiers as possible and document it - Izz al-Din al-Haddad</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military and Shin Bet: They said Haddad was killed in Gaza City’s Rimal neighborhood and accused him of overseeing hostage operations and issuing operational instructions to fighters before the Oct. 7 attacks. (<a href='https://www.ynetnews.com/article/ryqpr2r1mx'>Ynetnews</a>)</li><li>Hamas: It described Haddad as a central figure in directing combat operations and accused Israel of trying to achieve politically through killings what it had not achieved militarily. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40421489/israel-kills-hamas-leader-haddad-in-gaza-strike'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>Ceasefire overseer: WBUR reported that the ceasefire has seen both sides trade accusations of violations and that the top diplomat overseeing it said it had stalled over the deadlock on disarming Hamas. (<a href='https://www.wbur.org/news/2026/05/16/israeli-strike-kills-hamas-military-wing-leader-who-israel-says-was-an-architect-of-oct-7-attacks'>WBUR</a>)</li><li>Netanyahu government: Netanyahu told the weekly cabinet meeting that Hamas was in Israel’s grip and said Israel’s mission was to ensure Gaza would not pose a threat to Israel again. (<a href='https://www.annahar.com/arab-world/arabian-levant/310740/نتنياهو-إسرائيل-على-وشك-القضا-على-جميع-المسؤولين-عن-هجوم-7-أكتوبر'>Annahar</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353901/israels-pm-says-close-killing-all-architects-october-7-attack'>Israel’s PM says close to killing all architects of October 7 attack</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260517-most-of-the-architects-of-october-7-attacks-have-been-killed-says-netanyahu'>Most of the architects of October 7 attacks have been killed, says Netanyahu</a> - france24.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-pm-netanyahu-says-close-to-killing-all-architects-of-oct-7-attacks'>PM Netanyahu says Israel is close to killing all architects of Oct 7 attacks</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/izz-al-din-al-haddad-hamas-commander-killed-gaza-hamas-israel/'>Hamas leader who helped plan Oct. 7 attack